      "skill": "principle-fix-root-causes",
      "files": ["<change>"],
      "findings": [
        {
          "finding": "Root cause of the change-rule bug: changeMatch modeled its filters as early returns, so the first filter decided the result. The fix makes the filters a conjunction instead of adding a special case for commitSubject.",
          "cites": "Fix Root Causes",
          "commit": "2958652b9656",
          "patch": "cc94330a0f6de878408a52859cadfdf93d19672e"
        },
        {
          "finding": "Found in independent review: added-line rules never matched a path with a space, because git diff ends that \"+++ b/\" path with a tab. The new test failed with the skill missing, and passes after the tab is stripped. Paths that git still C-quotes, such as those with a tab or a double quote, are not handled.",
          "cites": "Fix Root Causes",
          "commit": "8113bfe",
          "patch": "1b4d4f869ee399691d84a3b27a32bf5293283065"
        },
        {
          "finding": "Second author pass: the root cause of the header misread is that the parser had no state for where a file header ends. The fix reads headers only between \"diff --git\" and the first \"@@\" instead of filtering lookalike paths. A search of tools/ found no other diff parser with the same flaw.",
          "cites": "Fix Root Causes",
          "commit": "58ed89f0cd6b",
          "patch": "7afd2f94fdc49b1754fbccae31ecc268baa7cb27"
        }
      ],
